# Agent quality gates (every substantive task)

Full scan narrative: `cursor-bundle/memory/feedback_agent_quality_gates_scan.md`

## Gate A — Workspace truth (before grep / KG / RCA)

1. Read `.cursor/workspace-kg-state.md` and `.cursor/git-workspace-state.json` (refresh: `bash scripts/bin/git-workspace-status.sh`).
2. `python3 cursor-bundle/kg/bin/kg.py validate && kg watermark` — note **provisional** repos and built `@sha` per repo.
3. If user/env names a **deployed branch or tag** → in **that repo**: `git fetch origin && git fetch upstream`, then read `upstream/<branch>` or tag — **not** assumed local checkout (`feedback_fetch_latest_before_checking_code.md`).

**Hard stop (state aloud before continuing):**

- Task is **integration/release** (DCF, disburse, LOS sync) but **any** money-path repo is on `feature/*` → run `sync_branches_v2.sh <train>` for task repos OR limit analysis to repos on the named train only.
- Task is **DPI** → `ensure-dpi-branches.sh` + `kg-switch` (`dpi-feature-branch-gate.mdc`).
- **Mixed trains** on disk (integration + feature/DPI across repos) → do not conclude cross-service contracts until aligned or scoped.

## Gate B — Flow domain (accounting)

Before editing or RCA on accounting money paths:

1. Resolve **apiName** (not folder guess).
2. `python3 cursor-bundle/kg/bin/kg.py flow <apiName>` then **read** `deploy/application/orchestration/*` for that request.
3. Check domain: `scripts/lib/accounting_flow_domains.json` — do not conflate:
   - `death_foreclosure` (`loanDeathForeclosure`) vs `foreclosure` (`individualChildLoanForeclosure`, simulation APIs)
   - Outstanding/claim (death-date snapshot) vs GL legs (approve posting / billing job_time)
   - DPI jobs vs interest accrual jobs
4. Brain orientation: `system_brain/flows/<topic>.md` when it exists — then **verify in Java** (brain can lag branch).

## Gate C — KG is not enough

After `kg orient` / `kg why`:

- [ ] Orchestration XML read for the request chain
- [ ] Every processor in the changed path grepped for callers / EC keys
- [ ] Money path: `.cursor/gaps-and-risks.md` High rows in area
- [ ] RCA: `scripts/db-local.sh` or user-named `db-qaN.sh` — label NOT VERIFIED if not run

`KG_STRICT=1` when branch drift or dirty trees possible.

## Gate D — Honest testing & JIRA

| Dev claims | Allowed only when |
|------------|-------------------|
| Result: Pass (scenario) | `ntest run` / script PASS **this session** |
| Workbook numbers match | Simulation or read-only SQL — say so |
| LAN xxxxx Pass | Live API/batch on that LAN after deploy/reset |
| All scenarios Pass | Count matches list; no pending QA-only items in Dev Test |
| `ORCH_SIBLING_SIM` / `PROCESSOR_MIRROR_SIM` Pass | Registry case with `verify_mode` ran this session; **never** label as full E2E / LAN Pass; cite stage blocker (see `code-backed-simulation-testing.mdc`) |

Ship: `workspace-close.sh --from-pending` — not compile-only. Do not pull unrelated registry cases (e.g. `dpic.foreclosure_sim` on death-FC-only edits). When full money E2E is blocked, use a **code-backed** sim case — not an unrelated disburse smoke fallback.

### Gate D-acceptance — QA acceptance is the bar, not a passing subset (fail-closed)

`cursor-bundle/memory/feedback_qa_acceptance_not_subset_verify.md` (SDCP-10199/TDPQA-72 QA embarrassment 2026-07-17).

**Never claim Pass / RESOLVED / QA-ready when the assert allows the exact QA fail mode.** A test that prints `OK …` / `WARN …` for a state QA rejects is a **FAIL**, not a Pass.

| Anti-pattern (forbidden as Pass) | Required instead |
|---|---|
| Assert prints "OK A2 netting" / "allow prin > amount" and passes | `amount == principal`/component, OR delta legs **documented** in product spec + assert checks the named legs |
| "a labd linked to force-bill exists" | **Dedicated** force-bill labd visibility; EMI-labd hijack (EMI txn_ref overwritten, amounts still EMI) must FAIL |
| Happy-path only e2e | Add **dirty / pre-existing state** fixture (e.g. pre-existing EMI labd) — production rows are not clean seeds |
| Parent/product-scope item silently dropped | Must be **Pass** or explicit **Out-of-scope-documented** |
| "webapp verified" (partial) | Verify the exact screen fields QA cites via **live webapp APIs**: `getLoanAccountSummaryDetails` (`interest_details.accrued/original`), `getLoanAccountOverviewDetails` (`account_number_list`), `getLoanAccountStatement` (`DFC_PRTL_BILL` / RSCH amounts) — see `feedback_webapp_verify_mandatory_ui_ships.md` |
| SQL-only `ui_fields` as "webapp" | `acceptance_coverage` requires WEBAPP_UI_FIELD_MARKERS on `downstream_ui` |
| "row was inserted" / status-200 / COMPLETED as proof | **Real-flow DB write validation** (`feedback_real_flow_db_write_validate.md`): run the actual orch/API/job, read the row back, assert **column values** for every touched money table; presence-only / SQL-only "should have inserted" fails closed |

Subset e2e (loan CLOSED, txn exists) is **not Done** while the acceptance shape QA cites is unproven. Debug-only relax flags (`ACCEPTANCE_STRICT=0`, `ALLOW_A2_NETTING_DISPLAY_DIFF=1`) **never** produce a handoff Pass.

**Machine gate:** `scripts/lib/acceptance_coverage.py` (+ manifest) — enforced domains must declare `acceptance.dimensions` / webapp-marker `ui_fields` **and value-level `acceptance.db_asserts` (or `expect.db_eq`) covering every `domain_money_tables` entry** on registry cases; wired into `ship_discipline_gate` / `ship-loop-gate`. Subset notes, SQL-only “webapp”, and presence-only DB asserts fail closed.

## Gate E — Outputs (RCA / JIRA / release)

- Diplomatic edge-case framing for RCA and QA comments (`jira-fix-update` skill).
- Tiered L0/L1 minimum for bugs (`tiered-solution-approach.mdc`).
- Minimal fix gate before propose (`minimal-fix-impact-gate.mdc`).

## Autopilot

Every substantive user message: `bash scripts/bin/workspace-autopilot.sh task "…"` — if classification changes (RCA → sync → fix), re-run gates for the **new** domain.
